{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:20986-1","published":"2026-03-30T15:24:20Z","modified":"2026-04-10T18:23:58.092302Z","related":["CVE-2025-12817","CVE-2025-12818"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-12817","CVE-2025-12818"],"summary":"Security update for postgresql13","details":"This update for postgresql13 fixes the following issues:\n\nSecurity fixes:\n\n- CVE-2025-12817: Fixed missing check for CREATE privileges\n  on the schema in CREATE STATISTICS allowed table owners to create\n  statistics in any schema, potentially leading to unexpected naming\n  conflicts (bsc#1253332)\n- CVE-2025-12818: Fixed several places in libpq were not\n  sufficiently careful about computing the required size of a memory\n  allocation. Sufficiently large inputs could cause integer overflow,\n  resulting in an undersized buffer, which would then lead to writing\n  past the end of the buffer (bsc#1253333)\n\nOther fixes:\n\n- Update to 13.23\n\n  * https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/p-3171/\n  * https://www.postgresql.org/docs/release/13.23\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"postgresql13","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/postgresql13&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Server%2016.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"13.23-160000.1.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"postgresql13":"13.23-160000.1.1","postgresql13-contrib":"13.23-160000.1.1","postgresql13-devel":"13.23-160000.1.1","postgresql13-docs":"13.23-160000.1.1","postgresql13-plperl":"13.23-160000.1.1","postgresql13-plpython":"13.23-160000.1.1","postgresql13-pltcl":"13.23-160000.1.1","postgresql13-server":"13.23-160000.1.1","postgresql13-server-devel":"13.23-160000.1.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:20986-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"postgresql13","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Server for SAP applications 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/postgresql13&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Serv